WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.890
- I drew on her back with my finger,

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:07.162
the letter I, and then
a heart, and then (sobs)

00:00:07.162 --> 00:00:07.995
- Aww, that's so cute.

00:00:07.995 --> 00:00:11.195
(soft music)

00:00:11.195 --> 00:00:12.770
(Alex sobs)

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.220
- Do you want me to reverse
that question on you?

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.053
- No

00:00:16.053 --> 00:00:16.886
(both laughing)

00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:18.269
- No, no, no, no.

00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:21.269
(soft upbeat music)

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.835
- Hi. How's it going?

00:00:26.835 --> 00:00:28.870
- Hi. (laughs) Hi.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:29.810
- My name's Alex.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.160
Nice to meet you.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.800
- Hi, I'm Krista.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:33.713
- My name's Casey.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.522
What's your name?

00:00:35.522 --> 00:00:36.355
- Karen.

00:00:36.355 --> 00:00:37.188
- Hi Karen.

00:00:37.188 --> 00:00:38.021
(Karen laughs)

00:00:38.021 --> 00:00:39.845
- Hi, my name's Jade.

00:00:39.845 --> 00:00:40.678
- Nice to meet you.

00:00:40.678 --> 00:00:41.511
I'm Michael.

00:00:41.511 --> 00:00:42.403
- Hi, Michael.

00:00:42.403 --> 00:00:44.902
- How are you doing, like really?

00:00:44.902 --> 00:00:47.319
(soft music)

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.380
(bird chips)

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.213
Can you hear me?

00:00:52.213 --> 00:00:53.587
- Yeah, I can hear you.

00:00:53.587 --> 00:00:54.420
- Yeah.

00:00:55.609 --> 00:00:56.943
- I'm doing better.

00:01:02.021 --> 00:01:02.854
It's been really rough.

00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:03.687
- Yeah.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.850
- I'm just trying hard to hang on

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:12.480
and live by the notion
of it is what it is.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.313
- Yeah.

00:01:13.313 --> 00:01:15.300
- And no matter what happens to me

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.700
it's good because I'll learn from it.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.430
Yeah. How about you?

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:21.854
How are you?

00:01:21.854 --> 00:01:23.710
(Karen laughs)

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:24.930
- The same thing.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.410
- Yeah.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.430
It's been hard for everybody.

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.310
- Yeah.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.080
- Are you getting better?

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.320
- Yeah. I think with the growing up,

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.880
there's a lot of things
I need to work through

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.483
just things I need to
learn from, but it's hard.

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:43.940
- It's hard sometimes

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.803
'cause the world moves so fast.

00:01:45.803 --> 00:01:46.845
- Yeah. (chuckles) Really.

00:01:46.845 --> 00:01:49.558
- And we see other people being good

00:01:49.558 --> 00:01:53.340
and getting it and we feel
like, why don't I get it?

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.233
- Yeah. Or like why can't I do that?

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.743
- We all have our moment,

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.200
we just have to be patient

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:04.816
and have faith that things
will work themselves out.

00:02:04.816 --> 00:02:08.540
as long as we keep doing
the next indicated thing

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.689
and trying to help people and be kind.

00:02:11.689 --> 00:02:13.140
- Yeah.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:18.140
- Well, I'm looking at my, I
guess ex-girlfriend right now.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.910
We still hang out as we're doing right now

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:27.529
and we still love each
other and we still...

00:02:27.529 --> 00:02:29.946
(soft music)

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.400
- Okay.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.233
- Sorry.

00:02:33.233 --> 00:02:37.943
- So how are you feeling
about all that then?

00:02:41.205 --> 00:02:42.693
- It is hard.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.733
- Okay. I get that.

00:02:47.098 --> 00:02:48.015
I get that.

00:02:50.483 --> 00:02:52.930
- It's hard to move on.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.703
Wow. I didn't know I was
gonna get (laughs) emotional.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.935
Geez. How are you doing really?

00:02:58.935 --> 00:03:01.352
(soft music)

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.970
- Today is a good day.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:07.430
Not every day is a good day,
but today is a good day.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.990
- Today's actually a
really, really good day.

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:12.530
Actually, the last couple
years have been really

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:17.000
really rough, too, but
today's been really great.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.040
So (laughs) yeah.

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:20.260
And I think it's on the up and up.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:22.100
- What's causing you hardship?

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.370
- I think the thing
that's hurting me the most

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.630
is my parents are immigrants,

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.072
they've just been finding
the immigration process,

00:03:28.072 --> 00:03:29.620
that's a long time.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.080
- Yeah.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:32.230
- And I think that's the one thing

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.110
that's kind of always
on my mind right now.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.250
- Do you live with them?

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.660
- Yeah.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.150
- Do you take care of them?

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.300
- Yeah. And they kind of had me

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.126
when they were kind of older.

00:03:43.126 --> 00:03:43.959
- Yeah.

00:03:43.959 --> 00:03:46.909
- So I want them to be able to
have that before they leave.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:51.691
- Yeah.

00:03:51.691 --> 00:03:54.360
- They just wanna go back
to where they came from

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:55.537
before they pass away.

00:03:55.537 --> 00:03:56.370
- Yeah.

00:03:58.351 --> 00:04:03.279
- And I feel like the
one thing that helps me

00:04:03.279 --> 00:04:07.028
every day is that when people
at work that are Mexican

00:04:07.028 --> 00:04:09.563
they come in and I can translate for them.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.380
That's something that kind of grounds me

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:15.280
back to knowing that I can help them.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.730
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.840
- What's something I
wouldn't believe about you?

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:22.673
- Wouldn't believe?

00:04:22.673 --> 00:04:23.506
- Yeah.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.730
- This one just came to mind.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:30.966
I'm kind of short, but
I'm good at basketball.

00:04:30.966 --> 00:04:32.620
(both laughing)

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.810
- Okay. Okay.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:34.700
This one always gets people

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.543
is that I've broken each arm five times.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.213
- Five times.

00:04:39.213 --> 00:04:40.046
(Jade laughs)

00:04:40.046 --> 00:04:40.879
- Yeah.

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:41.712
- Doing what?

00:04:41.712 --> 00:04:45.430
- Fallen off playgrounds,
snowboarding, skateboarding.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:46.410
- Okay. So your whole life?

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.261
- Yeah, just being reckless.

00:04:48.261 --> 00:04:49.094
( man chuckles)

00:04:49.094 --> 00:04:50.530
(Karen laughs)

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.690
- One time I had to go
home in kindergarten

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:55.180
'cause one of my friends
bite my butt cheek

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.200
so hard.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.222
- What?

00:04:57.222 --> 00:04:58.760
(Karen laughs)

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.133
I actually believe that.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:02.793
(Karen laughs)

00:05:02.793 --> 00:05:03.626
- Why?

00:05:03.626 --> 00:05:04.863
- 'Cause I don't think
you would make that up.

00:05:04.863 --> 00:05:06.779
(Karen laughs)

00:05:06.779 --> 00:05:07.810
(dog barks)

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:09.773
- What's something I
wouldn't believe about you?

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:13.650
- I'm fully fluent in Spanish.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:18.000
I can read it, write it,
speak it, understand it.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.118
I learned Spanish as a language
before I learned English.

00:05:22.118 --> 00:05:25.005
And I'm pretty much as white boys, I guess

00:05:25.005 --> 00:05:25.838
(Karen laughs)

00:05:25.838 --> 00:05:26.671
genetic white guy

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.560
but most people don't believe it.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:31.850
And then when I throw it out there

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.790
I always get really like ghost looks

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.967
or like big eyes, like, "Oh my goodness.

00:05:35.967 --> 00:05:37.233
"He said that?"

00:05:37.233 --> 00:05:38.066
(Karen chuckles)

00:05:38.066 --> 00:05:40.940
My grandmother who raised
me, she was my mom.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.442
She wanted to buy a house here

00:05:43.442 --> 00:05:46.860
in San Diego and opened
up a bed and breakfast.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:51.270
And she felt that it was
important for me to learn Spanish

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:54.010
because there's a lot of
Spanish speakers in San Diego.

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:56.640
And so I went to a school,
it was a magnet school.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:57.950
Everything was in Spanish.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:01.723
So I learned a lot about the Incas

00:06:01.723 --> 00:06:05.520
the (mumbles) the Mayans
and all those groups

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.920
more than I learned
about American history.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:08.753
- I'm glad.

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:11.810
- I wouldn't trade it for the world.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.190
I really appreciate the fact

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:14.329
that I can speak both languages.

00:06:14.329 --> 00:06:16.305
It's something I really cherish a lot.

00:06:16.305 --> 00:06:17.880
- Yeah.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.360
- Next question.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.330
What is your biggest insecurity?

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:25.500
- The first one I think
of is the way I talk

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:28.280
and you probably can't
tell from this interview

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.780
I'm actually kind of proud of myself

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.550
for keeping a conversation going.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:37.550
And so my biggest insecurity
is I mumble and I fumble

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:44.490
on my words and I have
these big ideas in my head

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:48.450
but I can't articulate them into words

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.720
and conversation and sentences.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.710
And I know I'm so smart in my head,

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:57.993
but I can't get it out.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:02.785
So maybe that's why I stay quiet a lot.

00:07:02.785 --> 00:07:04.570
(soft music)

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.770
- I don't feel like intelligence routes

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:11.300
from being able to speak everything

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:12.640
that you want your ideas.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:15.120
I mean, you could be the smartest person

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:17.354
and the quietest person.

00:07:17.354 --> 00:07:18.521
- That's true.

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:24.110
- Also your voice sounds nice to me.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.350
And if you have mumbled

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:27.520
or started or anything, I haven't noticed.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:30.240
- No. Yeah. Actually, I'm really happy

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.760
with how I am...

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:32.593
Yeah. I don't know.

00:07:32.593 --> 00:07:34.900
Maybe it's the surrounding the-

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.560
- Maybe it's just easier
to talk to a stranger.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.449
- That's true. Yeah.

00:07:38.449 --> 00:07:41.213
- Michael, what's your biggest insecurity?

00:07:41.213 --> 00:07:42.603
- Oh, biggest insecurity.

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:46.410
My voice probably, it's kind of monotone

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:49.640
and I can mumble and not
speak up all the time.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:51.890
So some days I'm okay at it

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.750
some days I'm really bad at it

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.210
and it's just kind of annoying

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:57.798
for the days whereas I just
can't get it to work right.

00:07:57.798 --> 00:07:58.631
(Michael chuckles)

00:07:58.631 --> 00:07:59.610
- Oh, well, if it's any console,

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:00.900
I thought your voice sounded nice.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:01.733
- Oh, thank you.

00:08:01.733 --> 00:08:02.610
- Yeah.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:04.719
- What's your biggest insecurity?

00:08:04.719 --> 00:08:09.010
- I feel like I just
don't like the way I look

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:12.763
that sounds cliche as a
girl, but I just don't.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.390
- What is a song that reminds
you of someone you love?

00:08:19.412 --> 00:08:21.662
(man sobs)

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.560
- I listen to a lot of music

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:37.136
and I attach emotions to songs.

00:08:37.136 --> 00:08:37.969
- Me too.

00:08:37.969 --> 00:08:39.410
- And when I listen to them

00:08:42.077 --> 00:08:44.480
(Man sobs)

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:47.750
I like to think that I'm time traveling

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:49.693
in my mind to places.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:55.110
And there's an artist called Laplux

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.843
and there's a song called "Without You"

00:09:01.848 --> 00:09:03.070
(man sobs)

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:08.070
and my mom passed away

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.173
about a month before my daughter
was born and it killed me.

00:09:15.097 --> 00:09:20.097
I was broken and this song

00:09:20.510 --> 00:09:22.410
is something I heard during that time.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:28.290
And I go to it just so that
I can feel that pain again

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:32.233
so I can feel something,
so I don't forget.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.423
I feel like as time goes by,

00:09:36.468 --> 00:09:38.473
she's drifting away from me.

00:09:39.644 --> 00:09:40.477
(dog barks)

00:09:40.477 --> 00:09:42.810
And so I really listen to that song

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:46.650
to try to still feel, even
though it's not necessarily

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:51.650
a good feeling, it's something
I'm sorry that I'm emotional.

00:09:51.943 --> 00:09:52.776
- It's okay.

00:09:52.776 --> 00:09:54.474
I really started crying
at the first question.

00:09:54.474 --> 00:09:55.334
(Karen laughs)

00:09:55.334 --> 00:09:56.297
- Yeah.
- I don't even know why.

00:09:56.297 --> 00:09:58.570
- What about yourself?

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:00.635
- My dad's really (sobs)

00:10:00.635 --> 00:10:02.120
my dad's really sweet.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.230
When I went through my
(mumbles) teen phase

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:05.840
I was listening to like Led Zeppelin

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:09.830
and he would always
play in the living room.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:11.630
He always listened to "Stairway to Heaven"

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:14.572
and I'm pretty sure it's
the only song he knows.

00:10:14.572 --> 00:10:16.810
'Cause me and my dad
are been very similar,

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:20.650
we don't talk a lot, but we
do a lot kind of non-verbally.

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:22.162
And I feel like a lot of the times,

00:10:22.162 --> 00:10:25.430
he just plays music in the
living room to comfort me

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.830
- Probably he cares a lot about you.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:31.663
- Yeah.

00:10:31.663 --> 00:10:33.784
- He probably thinks a lot about you

00:10:33.784 --> 00:10:35.180
and how you're feeling.

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:37.430
I can relate just with my own daughter

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:41.100
with our situation and us moving

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:44.330
and it's abruptly and there's
a lot of changes going on

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.823
and I really worry about
how she's taking it.

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:52.110
- I have two songs,
"Blank Space" and "Style."

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:56.250
Not because they're
relatable in the lyrics,

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:57.550
but my sister and I,

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:01.590
we would do road trips from
Canada to San Diego a few times.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:04.470
And there was one road
trip where the only song

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.500
in her phone was "Blank Space."

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.950
And then SiriusXM Radio wasn't working

00:11:09.950 --> 00:11:11.587
but they kept on playing "Style" so-

00:11:11.587 --> 00:11:13.241
- "Blank Space" like-

00:11:13.241 --> 00:11:14.074
- By Taylor Swift.
like Taylor Swift?

00:11:14.074 --> 00:11:15.022
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:11:15.022 --> 00:11:15.855
- (laughs) Okay.

00:11:15.855 --> 00:11:17.100
- And then "Style" is the other one.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.300
So we just went back and forth

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.790
- That's so funny.
for a 20 hour drive

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:20.623
with those two songs.

00:11:20.623 --> 00:11:21.897
- Oh my God.

00:11:21.897 --> 00:11:23.840
- Tell me about your first love

00:11:23.840 --> 00:11:26.410
and why did you fall in love with them?

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.436
- Damn, I'm gonna get emotional again.

00:11:28.436 --> 00:11:29.679
(Krista laughs)

00:11:29.679 --> 00:11:31.265
Well, I'm looking at
her like I said earlier.

00:11:31.265 --> 00:11:35.703
- Aww.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:39.670
You can take your time.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:40.503
It's okay.

00:11:40.503 --> 00:11:41.550
- Thank you.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.590
I've always been pretty
independent/introverted

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:48.200
and I never had a desire
to be with someone.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:52.430
Angel came around outta nowhere.

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:55.620
We clicked, and I told her I loved her

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.570
in the first month.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:59.530
And I don't think I told her actually,

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:00.871
now that I'm remembering it.

00:12:00.871 --> 00:12:04.060
I drew on her back with my finger,

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:05.900
the letter I, and then a heart

00:12:05.900 --> 00:12:06.733
and then it...

00:12:07.723 --> 00:12:10.223
(Krista sobs)

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:14.143
- Aww, that's so cute.

00:12:17.837 --> 00:12:20.170
(Alex sobs)

00:12:35.993 --> 00:12:36.843
- You doing okay?

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.720
- It is good to talk about this

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:42.998
and it's good to let it out.

00:12:42.998 --> 00:12:43.831
- Yeah.

00:12:45.713 --> 00:12:47.630
- It's good to tell the world, too

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:51.700
but also just to tell a stranger

00:12:52.592 --> 00:12:54.820
and I know she's watching me right now

00:12:55.945 --> 00:12:56.845
and tell her, too.

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:05.420
Do you want me to reverse
that question on you?

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:06.420
- No.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:07.390
(both laughing)

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.620
- No, no, no, no.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:09.453
No, no.

00:13:09.453 --> 00:13:10.400
You're okay

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:11.233
- Man.

00:13:12.802 --> 00:13:13.635
- [Woman] Are you okay?

00:13:13.635 --> 00:13:14.837
- Ugly crying on camera.

00:13:14.837 --> 00:13:16.830
(both laughing)

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.140
- You're okay.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:22.303
- She's a good listener
and picks a good stranger.

00:13:22.303 --> 00:13:24.830
(woman laughs)

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:25.746
- Thank you.

00:13:25.746 --> 00:13:28.070
- Okay. Tell me a secret, Michael.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:28.903
- A secret.

00:13:28.903 --> 00:13:29.848
- Yeah.

00:13:29.848 --> 00:13:31.250
- Geez. I don't know
if I have any secrets.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:32.330
Let me think.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.190
- I actually do have a secret to share.

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:37.200
I'm sorry, but deep down,

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:42.200
nobody knows this but I
wanna be able to sing karaoke

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:44.193
really well.

00:13:44.193 --> 00:13:45.038
- Me, too.

00:13:45.038 --> 00:13:49.390
- And I envision singing the song

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.710
and then everybody getting up and clapping

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:54.790
but I sound so horrible on a microphone.

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:56.471
And I see my blue car coming.

00:13:56.471 --> 00:13:57.304
- [Woman] Okay.

00:13:57.304 --> 00:13:58.137
- No.

00:13:58.137 --> 00:13:59.450
- [Woman] Say something
kind about the other person

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:00.880
based on your conversation.

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:03.730
- You seem like a very
genuine, sincere person

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.490
that wants to help people.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:07.580
And I hope that you're
able to stay focused

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:10.418
on that because everything
else is accessory,

00:14:10.418 --> 00:14:12.433
it's all about our passions.

00:14:13.743 --> 00:14:14.690
- Thank you.

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:17.590
- I notice that you're
really good at listening

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:20.120
and you heard me and you understood me.

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:21.600
So thank you.

00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:22.790
- Thank you.

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:24.400
You have a very big heart.

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:26.390
You're definitely very full of love.

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:29.990
- Wow.
- And you have a lot of love

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:33.093
and a lot of kindness
and warmth inside of you.

00:14:34.553 --> 00:14:35.386
You also cried a little bit,

00:14:35.386 --> 00:14:38.010
so that's why I picked up on that one

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:41.290
'cause you're definitely,
definitely full of love.

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:42.123
- Well, you know what?

00:14:42.123 --> 00:14:47.123
That really means a lot,
'cause besides maybe Angel

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:50.490
I don't think anyone's said that to me.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.320
So that means a lot.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.620
- Honestly this really made my day.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:56.720
You're just such a cool person to talk to.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.215
And I do like your voice by the way.

00:14:59.215 --> 00:15:00.083
(both laughing)

00:15:00.083 --> 00:15:01.040
- That all means a lot.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.200
Yeah. Thank you.

00:15:02.200 --> 00:15:05.670
I'll just say even though
I know I satisfied my part,

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.000
but my voice, if I felt like you're...

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.000
I really like your voice.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.500
I know the headphones probably
make it sound really good,

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:12.890
but this is nice and smooth

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.470
and I really enjoyed
how much you opened up

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:17.640
about your family and your past.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:18.580
It was a fun conversation.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:19.510
Yeah, definitely.

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:20.343
- Yeah.

00:15:20.343 --> 00:15:23.165
- [Man] Whenever you're ready,
you can definitely turn.

00:15:23.165 --> 00:15:25.498
(dog barks)

00:15:27.239 --> 00:15:29.822
(Karen laughs)

00:15:32.872 --> 00:15:33.705
- How's it going?

00:15:33.705 --> 00:15:34.538
- Hi.

00:15:34.538 --> 00:15:35.371
(both laughing)

00:15:35.371 --> 00:15:36.204
- How are you?

00:15:36.204 --> 00:15:37.037
- Good.

00:15:37.037 --> 00:15:37.870
- It's nice to see you.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:38.703
- Yeah, it was fun.

00:15:38.703 --> 00:15:39.536
- Yeah, it was.

00:15:39.536 --> 00:15:40.369
This is really cool.

00:15:40.369 --> 00:15:41.202
- Yeah.

00:15:41.202 --> 00:15:44.301
(both laughing)

00:15:44.301 --> 00:15:45.134
- Hi.

00:15:45.134 --> 00:15:45.967
- Hi.

00:15:45.967 --> 00:15:46.800
- Nice to meet you.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:47.633
- Me, too.

00:15:47.633 --> 00:15:48.466
- Was it...

00:15:48.466 --> 00:15:49.620
We talked so much.

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:50.607
Was it Krista?

00:15:50.607 --> 00:15:51.440
- Yes.

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:52.273
Oh, wow. Great.

00:15:52.273 --> 00:15:53.106
- Alex.

00:15:53.106 --> 00:15:53.939
- Yes.

00:15:53.939 --> 00:15:54.772
- Thank you.

00:15:54.772 --> 00:15:55.605
- Yeah.

00:15:55.605 --> 00:15:56.723
- Nice to meet you.

00:15:56.723 --> 00:15:58.205
- Every time I watch my interview videos,

00:15:58.205 --> 00:15:59.766
I was like if I'm in
Balboa Park and I see her

00:15:59.766 --> 00:16:01.121
I'm gonna act like I don't know her.

00:16:01.121 --> 00:16:01.954
- Glad you did it.

00:16:01.954 --> 00:16:03.066
- So I'll do it.

00:16:03.066 --> 00:16:03.899
But no, (laughs) I couldn't hold it in.

00:16:03.899 --> 00:16:05.330
I was like, I know you.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:06.820
I know who you are.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:09.090
I was like, please still take me.

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:11.020
- Wait. Angel, do you
mind getting in this?

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:12.901
I'm sure everyone's curious.

00:16:12.901 --> 00:16:14.143
- Yes.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:16.475
